Description: Offer KDE's org_kde_kwin_appmenu protocol and give the menu address of a window to the Shell.
 Chromium, Firefox and Qt name the D-Bus address of the com.canonical.dbusmenu menu of a Wayland window with
 org_kde_kwin_appmenu, which KWin offers, and a shell can then show the menu of the focused window in its own
 panel. Mutter keeps the address on the surface, because a client can name it before the surface has a
 window, and gives it to the Shell as the MetaWindow properties dbus-appmenu-service-name and
 dbus-appmenu-object-path, which are notified when the address changes. Destroying the appmenu object
 withdraws the address it named, since the protocol has clients remove the object when they no longer offer a
 menu. The protocol XML is a copy of src/protocols/appmenu.xml of plasma-wayland-protocols (MIT license).
 .
 The test wayland-kde-appmenu has a client name an address, name it again unchanged, change it and release
 it, and checks the getters, the properties and their notifications after each step.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
